   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1948-12-16">December 16, 1948</date></dateline>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Prof
                  Tillich</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>I am indeed completely in your debt for the splendid promise you made to be a member
               of our Clinic on Evangelism faculty next June. This note will verify the dates – June
               20th to 24th.</p>
            <p>I cannot tell you the enthusiasm which your promise generated among our men. I can only
            trust that nothing will intervene which will prevent your coming.</p>
            <p>I shall provably be in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York</rs> sometime during the winter
            and shall stop by and speak with you further.</p>
            <p>I trust you have forgotten my family intrusion the other evening.</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Our very best wishes to you,<lb/>Sincerely,</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5405" type="person"><hi rend="hand">Lloyd C.
                        Wicke</hi></rs></signed>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Prof. Paul Johannes Tillich,
                  D.D.</rs><lb/>Union Theological Seminary<lb/>Broadway at 120th Street<lb/><rs
                  ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York 27, New York</rs><lb/>LCW/r
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
